      "writtenOn": "2022-01-13T23:00:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The AIDL annotation is used to generate the checks in the Java stub. The Java annotation is used as a visibility marker for engineers to see that a permission check has already been performed.\n\nThere is another change underway (ag/16602924) to confirm that the same annotation is used on any derived class from the Stub. \n\nIn the end, this allows us to: require annotations when defining a new interface, have the same annotation trickle down on any implementation and have a clear indicator of which permissions are already verified when editing the implementation.",
      "parentUuid": "9d475c08_d3163df8",
